(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["me-easy-2026-001"]={"v":1,"id":"me-easy-2026-001","title":"Advance Level Test-1 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME","sourceTitle":"Advance Level Test-1 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME","branch":"MECHANICAL ENGINEERING","code":"ME","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2026 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering","seriesId":"me-easy-2026","num":1,"category":"advance","year":"2026","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering"},"source":"MECHANICAL ENGINEERING/MADE EASY/GATE_2026_+_GATE_2025_Online_Test_Series_Mechanical_Engineering/002_Advance Level Test-1 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In a certain code language, if the word DISTANCE is coded as EDCINSAT then ACQUIRE is coded as</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"EACIQUR"},{"key":"B","html":"EACRIUQ"},{"key":"C","html":"ERCIAQV"},{"key":"D","html":"EARCIQU"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5fe9736615c288b82d2c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":2,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p><em>ABCDEF</em> is a regular hexagon of side 6 cm. What is the area of triangle <em>BDF</em>?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6a22ffd774219aa27a5b.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/b4/b4fa9c27cc2c1caa850b.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/0c/0c08c66c1f19cbc67c8b.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"24 cm<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/dc/dc7eb4147dc1f339f726.png\" /></div>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>If log<sub>3</sub> 2, log<sub>3</sub>(2 <sup>x</sup> – 5) and log<sub>3</sub> (2 <sup>x</sup> – 7/2) are in <em>AP</em>, then <em>x</em> is equal to</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2"},{"key":"B","html":"3"},{"key":"C","html":"4"},{"key":"D","html":"either of (a) or (b)"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8a/8ae6cdc1a7d189aa3978.png\" /></div>"},{"n":4,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In a group of 132 people; 50, 60, 70 people like different sweets – Barfi, Jalebi, Rasgulla respectively. The number of people who like all the three sweets is half the number of people who like exactly 2 sweets. The number of people who like Barfi and Jalebi only, Jalebi and Rasgulla only and Barfi and Rasgulla only is same. The number of people who like all the three sweets are ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[12,12],"answerText":"12","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>12 (12 - 12)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/ea8c54977dece4b4087e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":5,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p><em>x</em>, 17, 3<em>x</em> – y – 2 and 3<em>x</em> + y – 30 are 4 consecutive terms of an arithmetic progression. The value of <em>x</em> + y is ________ .</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[29,29],"answerText":"29","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>29 (29 - 29)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/91/91658d8291ce4606b18e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":6,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>If a , <em>a<sub>2</sub></em> , <em>a <sub>3</sub></em> ........... <em>a<sub>n</sub></em> are in <em>AP</em>, where a <sub>i</sub> > 0 for all <em>i</em>, then the value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/397aacdd92a34268a90c.png\" /> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/86/8626bf209cdb4cf101d6.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2a/2ad7019b59739919bbbc.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/23/23bf1db9fdfdec840ddb.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c7/c7dbfe8b9c055379c16a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":7,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Karan and Arjun run a 100 m race, where Karan beats Arjun by 10 m. To do a favour to Arjun, Karan starts 10 m behind the starting line in a second 100 m race. They both run at earlier speeds.<br />\nWhich of the following is true in connection with the second race?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Karan and Arjun reach the finishing line simultaneously."},{"key":"B","html":"Arjun beats Karan by 1 m"},{"key":"C","html":"Arjun beats Karan by 1.1 m"},{"key":"D","html":"Karan beats Arjun by 1 m"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c6/c68c7ab35d1bbe567389.png\" /></div>"},{"n":8,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Select the correct mirror image of the given figure when the mirror is placed to the right side of the figure.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2b/2b948fd6289623b9672d.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7d/7dc04f6635f76ca5741d.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3e/3eab4e6dc7d14c9e0663.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a1/a1036a95a96007c16fd2.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7c/7c9356741e21398db381.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Choose the pair of words which have a relationship between themselves which is similar to the relationship between the given pair:<br />\nSQUANDER : MONEY ::</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"trespass : property"},{"key":"B","html":"dally : time"},{"key":"C","html":"procrastinate : task"},{"key":"D","html":"accomplish : success"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\n(CAUSE AND EFFECT) When one squanders, one wastes money, when one dallies, one wastes time.</p>"},{"n":10,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In film and videotape, it is possible to induce viewers to project their feelings onto characters on the screen. In one study, when a camera shot of a woman’s face was preceded by a shot of a baby in a crib, the audience thought the woman’s face was registering happiness. When the same shot of the woman’s face was preceded by a shot of a lion running toward the camera, the audience thought the woman’s face was registering fear. Television news teams must be careful to avoid such manipulation of their viewers.<br />\nWhich of the following can be inferred from the passage?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Television news teams have abused their position of trust in the past"},{"key":"B","html":"The expression on the woman’s face was, in actuality, blank."},{"key":"C","html":"A camera shot of a baby in a crib provoked feelings of happiness in the audience."},{"key":"D","html":"Audiences should strive to be less gullible."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nThis is an inference question. The test writers are probably not interested in the conclusion of the passage. Considering the given options, we&rsquo;ll look for a statement that seems so obvious that it almost doesn&rsquo;t need saying.<br />\n&bull; Television news teams have abused their position of trust in the past. If you chose this answer,<br />\nyou inferred too much. The passage doesn&rsquo;t say that news teams have ever abused their position<br />\nof trust. Eliminate it.<br />\n&bull; The expression on the woman&rsquo;s face was, in actuality, blank. The audience had no idea what<br />\nthe expression on the woman&rsquo;s face was, and neither do we.<br />\n&bull; A camera shot of a baby in a crib provoked feelings of happiness in the audience. This is the<br />\nbest answer. The passage says that the audience projects its own feelings onto characters on<br />\nthe screen. If the audience believes the woman&rsquo;s face reflects happiness, then that must have<br />\nbeen its own reaction.<br />\n&bull; Audiences should strive to be less gullible. Rather it suggests Television news teams to be<br />\ncareful to avoid manipulation of their viewers. This statement goes way beyond the intent of the passage.<br />\nHence, option (c) is correct.</p>"},{"n":11,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A structural member under loading undergoes uniform plane stress condition. At a critical point in the member, the state of stress is as shown in the figure.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5ff481d57f79f6db1c02.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The yield strength of material in shear is 200 MPa and Poisson ratio 0.3. If the component is designed using Haigh’s total strain energy theory, the factor of safety is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1.67"},{"key":"B","html":"0.95"},{"key":"C","html":"1.53"},{"key":"D","html":"1.03"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1e/1e1b920f491331d6a17a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":12,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A straight cylindrical bar of 20 mm diameter and 1.5 m long is freely supported at its two ends in a horizontal position and loaded at the centre with the concentrated load of 100 N. The central deflection is 6 mm. If the bar is now placed vertically and loaded along its axis, then ratio</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/2f/2f7ec2831415eb483663.png\" /> (<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/9a/9abe93a9fc4dfb7e581f.png\" /> are the maximum stresses in two cases) is<br />\n </div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0.343"},{"key":"B","html":"1.812"},{"key":"C","html":"0.56"},{"key":"D","html":"2.92"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b8/b8d3cb867388e1eedc8a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Three forces are acting in a plane as shown in figure. The moment of the net force about point <em>A</em> is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f3/f31aefae64a68fcb8571.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1214.2 N-m"},{"key":"B","html":"1614.2 N-m"},{"key":"C","html":"2628.427 N-m"},{"key":"D","html":"3026.427 N-m"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6bbfd615df8cf060fba4.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4e/4e798803b2bfa1bdbb9e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>An open tank has 2.0 m height and it contains water upto a depth of 1.8 m. How high must its side be (in m) if no water to be spilled out when subjected to horizontal acceleration of 4.5 m/s?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/da/da482a40160fcccbebf3.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2.3 m"},{"key":"B","html":"2.0 m"},{"key":"C","html":"1.8 m"},{"key":"D","html":"5.7 m"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/59/5994d7d63f670fddde82.png\" /></div>"},{"n":15,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A 35 mm × 35 mm square blank is to be cut from a sheet metal of 2 mm thick. If the percentage penetration is 25% of the material thickness and ultimate shear stress of material is 280 N/mm<sup>2</sup>, then the workdone required is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"156.8 J"},{"key":"B","html":"19.6 J"},{"key":"C","html":"78.4 J"},{"key":"D","html":"39.2 J"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9f/9f120fcadd86dba573cc.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b1/b15867f1b19cd37f8f8b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":16,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A steam power-plant employs a wet type cooling tower. It receives warm water at 30°C at rate of 1 kg of water per kg of air. Air enters tower at 20°C DBT and 60% RH leaves at 28°C DBT 90% RH.<br />\nMakeup water is added at 20°C.<br />\nRefer the following data:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7d/7d73577774466c5ed457.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The temperature of water leaving the cooling tower is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"10°C"},{"key":"B","html":"20°C"},{"key":"C","html":"30°C"},{"key":"D","html":"40°C"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/85/85e5aa99a0e9d0b56649.png\" /></div>"},{"n":17,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A self-aligning ball bearing has a dynamic load capacity of 33.5 kN (that is, a rating of 33.5 kN such that 90% of a group bearings will last 500 hours at 1800 rev/min). If the equivalent radial load actually applied to the bearing is 44.5 kN. What is the average life in hours that can be expected?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"3.95 hours"},{"key":"B","html":"3.45 hours"},{"key":"C","html":"19.75 hours"},{"key":"D","html":"17.25 hours"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c8/c87ca1ad69daa448bf65.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/69/69cf47a1b34194c085b4.png\" /></div>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>1 kg of air is compressed reversibly and adiabatically from 80 kPa and 60°C to 0.4 MPa and is then expanded at constant pressure to the original volume. The net change in entropy for whole path is. (Take <em>C<sub>V</sub></em> = 0.7 kJ/kgK)</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1153 J/K"},{"key":"B","html":"1127 J/K"},{"key":"C","html":"1027 J/K"},{"key":"D","html":"923 J/K"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1b/1bd566667a57d9774b33.png\" /></div>"},{"n":19,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A spray cooling coil is used to cool and dehumidify air under the following conditions:<br />\nAir inlet condition : 27°C DBT and 20°C WBT<br />\nSpecific enthalpy = 65 kJ/kg of dry air, specific volume is 0.855 m<sup>3</sup>/kg<br />\nAir output condition : 12°C DBT and 8°C WBT<br />\nSpecific enthalpy = 20 kJ/kg of dry air<br />\nThe total amount of air flow is 1795 m<sup>3</sup>/min and the chilled water inlet and outlet temperatures are 8°C and 13°C respectively. The mass flow rate of the chilled water is<br />\n[Take specific heat capacity of water = 4.2 kJ/kgK]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"75 kg/min"},{"key":"B","html":"4500 kg/min"},{"key":"C","html":"2100 kg/min"},{"key":"D","html":"35 kg/min"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e3/e3ac31de60d28b56ebd2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":20,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A six cylinder, four stroke diesel engine develops 120 kW at 2500 rpm. The fuel to be injected per cycle per cylinder is 0.058 cc. If the specific gravity of the fuel is 0.8, then the brake specific fuel consumption is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"174 kg/kWh"},{"key":"B","html":"174 g/kWh"},{"key":"C","html":"464 g/kWh"},{"key":"D","html":"348 kg/kWh"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9a/9a21644e0c1d0059c208.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":21,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The directional derivative of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/cf/cf780154c0675ba6f66d.png\" /> in the direction of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/bf/bfdee504254440e0239e.png\" /> will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/fd/fd44d20207c4990cafdb.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/7e/7e13fd1a066ef76c954d.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/2c/2c7f1fa06254ff99438a.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/74/74cb3e105820acd7e053.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f6bd939a3e8633f6c120.png\" /></div>"},{"n":22,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The solution of differential equation <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/a0/a0193abd1a50a045f822.png\" /> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bb848e8477ace97416d4.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/22/2208f17cf03147905adb.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/18b2975ed5bcef374104.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/35/35dcf4ee361f1d747025.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/71/7125a1c9c578e47ac94a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0f/0fcccc18f68e8f7d5932.png\" /></div>"},{"n":23,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Taylor’s tool life equation is given by <em>VT<sup>n</sup></em> = <em>C</em>, where cutting speed V is in m/min, tool life is in min and exponent n is 0.25. If at a cutting speed of 60 m/min the tool life is of 1 hour and 20 minutes, then the cutting speed for a tool life of 1 hour will be_____ m/min. [Round off to one decimal place]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[64.2,64.8],"answerText":"64.5","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>64.5 (64.2 - 64.8)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/73/7339455672b4b2616185.png\" /></div>"},{"n":24,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Two compartment A and B of the tank are closed and filled with air and a fluid shown in figure below. The fluid having the specific gravity of 0.6. If the pressure gauge reads 4 kPa and weight of air is negligible, the manometer reading <em>h</em> (in cm) will be _____. (Round off to nearest integer)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/89/89d38f1d24fcc7096478.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[200,205],"answerText":"202","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>202 (200 - 205)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/97/976a4edb70f901ae749a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":25,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A solid square bar of length 6 m is used as a column with both ends fixed. If the end conditions are changed to one end fixed and other end free then the percentage change in the Euler’s crippling load of the column will be _____. [Round off to two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-93.99,-93.01],"answerText":"-93.75","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-93.75 (-93.99 - -93.01)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9b/9b3f856947c3ef8fb865.png\" /></div>"},{"n":26,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A thin hollow cylinder of 7 cm diameter and 11 cm length. If the radiant shape factor of the circular surface of this cylinder is 0.18 with respect to each other, then the shape factor of the curved surface of the cylinder with respect to itself is _______. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.72,0.76],"answerText":"0.74","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.74 (0.72 - 0.76)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4d/4d8d6fbb502518eb25e4.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bc/bc289782f00dc80a6b39.png\" /></div>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A structure along with the loads applied on it is shown in the figure below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3f/3f3d3a48dbd8d92bdd72.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The magnitude of force in the member <em>AB</em> is ____ kN. [Rounded off to nearest integer]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[25,25],"answerText":"25","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>25 (25 - 25)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5ef4622848d622ce316b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":28,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>In an inline slider crank mechanism the crank radius is 9 cm and the connecting rod length is 52 cm. If net effective piston force at 90° of the crank rotation from inner dead centre is 957 kN, then the magnitude of the crankshaft bearing reaction is _____ kN. [Round off to two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[167.95,168.37],"answerText":"168.17","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>168.17 (167.95 - 168.37)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/df/dfbe2e2406c9a2dade89.png\" /></div>"},{"n":29,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>For an activity, the optimistic, pessimistic and most likely times are 3, 13 and 8 days respectively.<br />\nThe probability of completing the project before 9.4 days is ________%. [Rounded off to the nearest integer]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[79,81],"answerText":"80","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>80 (79 - 81)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d82aabc6d665c5bf08b9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":30,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>An SI engine develops 70 kW of indicated power at full load. Its brake specific fuel consumption is 0.28 kg/kWh. At 60% load, the mechanical efficiency is 50%. Assuming constant frictional losses, the indicated specific fuel consumption at full load is ________ kg/kWh. (Correct upto three decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.173,0.175],"answerText":"0.175","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.175 (0.173 - 0.175)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4c62d3150a47f3a693cc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":31,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The demand for six consecutive months for a product are 10, 12, 11, 15, 13, 9 respectively. Using the three-month simple moving average forecasting method, the Bias for last three months is _______. [Round off to two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.1,0.12],"answerText":"0.11","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.11 (0.10 - 0.12)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0d/0ddc9b102ca044f7ef3a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/71/7103dd9e56f36e82b1f4.png\" /></div>"},{"n":32,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The monthly demand for an item is 800 units. If the annual procurement cost is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/df/dfbf66d0c8d711bc17eb.png\" /> and the economic order quantity is 640 units. Then the inventory Carrying cost per unit per month is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/e6/e6e146d91e250d2e8bfa.png\" /> _______ [Round off to three decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.146,0.166],"answerText":"0.156","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.156 (0.146 - 0.166)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/eb/eb88be92d6f7a69fe487.png\" /></div>"},{"n":33,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The inside and outside diameter of a hollow spherical shell are 1.2 m and 1.6 m respectively. The shell stores a liquid at 270°C, while the outside surface temperature of the shell is 90°C. If the thermal conductivity of shell, <em>k</em> = 48(1 + 2 × 10<sup>–3</sup> × <em>T</em> ) where, T is in degree Celsius and the ambient temperature of air is 27°C. [Neglect the radiation heat transfer]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The outside heat transfer coefficient is 700 W/m<sup>2</sup>K."},{"key":"B","html":"The outside heat transfer coefficient is 777 W/m<sup>2</sup>K."},{"key":"C","html":"The rate of heat conduction is 354.38 kW."},{"key":"D","html":"The rate of heat conduction is 254.38 kW."}],"answer":["A","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/34a5b6af253d412fa80b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/02/024f21454807ac2277c7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":34,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following statements is/are correct corresponding to impulse and reaction machines?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"For impulse machine the change in static head in the rotor is zero."},{"key":"B","html":"The lawn sprinkler is an example of impulse machine."},{"key":"C","html":"A paddle wheel rotated by the impingement of water from a stationary nozzle is an example of reaction machine."},{"key":"D","html":"The ratio of energy transfer by the change in static head to the total energy transfer in the rotor is as the degree of reaction."}],"answer":["A","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, d)<br />\nThe relative proportion of energy transfer obtained by the change in static head and by the<br />\nchange in dynamic head is one of the important factors for classifying fluid machines. The machine<br />\nfor which the change in static head in the rotor is zero is known as an impulse machine. The<br />\nparameter characterising the proportion of changes in the dynamic and static head in the rotor of<br />\na fluid machine is known as the degree of reaction and is defined as the ratio of energy transfer<br />\nby the change in the static head to the total energy transfer in the rotor. A very simple example of<br />\nan impulse machine is a paddle wheel rotated by the impingement of water from a Stationary<br />\nnozzle. A simple example of reaction machine can be shown by the familiar lawn sprinkler.</p>"},{"n":35,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The directional derivative of <em>xy</em><sup>3</sup>z<sup>2</sup> at the point (1, 1, –1) in the direction of the tangent to the curve <em>x</em> = <em>e<sup>t</sup></em>, <em>y</em> = sin2<em>t</em> + 1, z = 1 – cost at <em>t</em> = 0, is ________ .</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3,3.25],"answerText":"3.13","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3.13 (3.00 - 3.25)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/92/9228b675716fd01d9b13.png\" /></div>"},{"n":36,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A rolling disc of radius ‘<em>r</em>’ and mass ‘<em>m</em>’ is connected using two springs of stiffness ‘<em>s</em>’ and ‘2s’ as shown in the figure.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/df/dff96a6fd1026f774b8a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The natural frequency of the system for small rotation of disc is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/2649960267b254296a89.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/00/003bda465c59c6306f56.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/73/73adc1fd699961f56844.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/83659e62fc2378c863ac.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b4/b41bbc32ee8bba584f2c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2c/2cc2990ac5c3bc1115b9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":37,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following APT program is incorrect regarding entities shown in figure below?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/70/7040dbc674ee4df2de62.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"C4 = CIRCLE/ YSMALL, LN1, YSMALL, LN2, RADIUS,30"},{"key":"B","html":"C1 = CIRCLE/ XSMALL, LN1, YSMALL, LN2, RADIUS,10"},{"key":"C","html":"C2 = CIRCLE/ YLARGE, LN1, YLARGE, LN2, RADIUS,10"},{"key":"D","html":"P = POINT/ INTOF, LN1, LN2"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nP = POINT/ INTOF, LN1, LN2<br />\nC1 = CIRCLE/ XSMALL, LN1, YLARGE, LN2, RADIUS,10<br />\nC2 = CIRCLE/ YLARGE, LN1, YLARGE, LN2, RADIUS,10<br />\nC3 = CIRCLE/ YSMALL, LN2, XLARGE, LN1, RADIUS,10<br />\nC4 = CIRCLE/ YSMALL, LN1, YSMALL, LN2, RADIUS,30</p>"},{"n":38,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>One mole of an ideal gas undergoes two different cyclic processes I and II, as shown in the P-V diagram below. In Cycle I, processes <em>a</em>, <em>b</em>, <em>c</em> and <em>d</em> are isobaric, isothermal, isobaric and isochoric respectively. In cycle II, processes <em>a</em>′, <em>b</em>′, <em>c</em>′ and <em>d</em>′ are isothermal, isochoric, isobaric and  sochoric respectively.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/97/97e079ae22b72c1628ae.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The total work done during cycle-I is <em>W<sub>I</sub></em> and that during cycle II is <em>W<sub>II</sub></em>. The ratio <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/71/712dcd997a022acf048d.png\" /> is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"5"},{"key":"B","html":"4"},{"key":"C","html":"3"},{"key":"D","html":"2"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/58/58350330e0027591e1b7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/83c6fbcde14d572dd50d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":39,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A compound shaft of circular cross-section is made up of two different materials as shown in the figure.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7f/7f18e45a72a7e2a7852c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If a torque of 200 Nm is applied at point B, the maximum shear stress developed in the compound shaft is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"10 MPa"},{"key":"B","html":"15 MPa"},{"key":"C","html":"25 MPa"},{"key":"D","html":"35 MPa"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/00/0060851c6d5c55415bbf.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b4/b4da7986ea2a62845e08.png\" /></div>"},{"n":40,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A Joule cycle operates with air as the working fluid. The maximum temperature in the cycle is 1600 K, while the temperature and pressure before compression are 400 K and 1 bar. If the pressure ratio is 8, then the mean-effective pressure of the cycle is<br />\n[Take γ = 1.5 and R = 0.3 kJ/kgK, <em>c<sub>p</sub></em> = 1 kJ/kgK]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2 MPa"},{"key":"B","html":"190.5 kPa"},{"key":"C","html":"22 bar"},{"key":"D","html":"1.2 bar"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/98/98e5cb320e8ab70bcca7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d0/d01299fce63ac4072d63.png\" /></div>"},{"n":41,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Copper and nickel are found to form an alloy, more specifically a substitutional solid solution.<br />\nThese two elements are completely soluble in one another at all proportions. Which of the following reasons can not be attributed to the formation of such an alloy?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The atomic radii of Cu and Ni atoms are approximately the same."},{"key":"B","html":"Both Cu and Ni have FCC crystal structure."},{"key":"C","html":"Cu is electropositve while Ni is electronegative favouring the formation of alloy."},{"key":"D","html":"Most common valences is +1 for Cu and +2 for Ni."}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nThere are several features of the solute and solvent atoms that determine the degree to which the former dissolves in the latter, as follows:<br />\n1. Atomic size factor, appreciable quantities of a solute may be accomodated in this type of solid solution only when the difference in atomic radii between the two atom types is less than about &plusmn;15%. Otherwise, the solute atoms will create substantial lattice distortions and a new phase will form.<br />\n2. Crystal structure, for appreciable solid solubility the crystal structures for metals of both atom types must be the same.<br />\n3. Electronegativity, the more electropositive one element and the more electronegative the other, the greater is the likelihood that they will form an intermetallic compound instead of a substitutional solid solution.<br />\n4. Valences, other factors being equal, a metal will have more of a tendency to dissolve another metal of higher valency than one of a lower valency:<br />\nHence, option (c) is incorrect as Cu and Ni have similar electronegativities (1.9 and 1.8 respectively)</p>"},{"n":42,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The annulus gear <em>A</em> to be fixed gear, <em>P</em> and <em>C</em> constitute a compound planet having 25 and 15 teeth respectively. The figure shows a reduction gear with the input gear S having 25 teeth and output gear <em>D</em>. If all the gears are of the same pitch, then the speed ratio of the reduction gear is ____.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/67/6776d0c0f0997d9bb3cb.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"12"},{"key":"B","html":"15"},{"key":"C","html":"13"},{"key":"D","html":"14"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ac/ace50ee10e9690a198e3.png\" /></div>"},{"n":43,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Match <strong>List I (Machining processes)</strong> with <strong>List II (Applications)</strong> and select the correct answer using the codes given below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1f03183c9aa3b69beeb1.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"P-4, Q-2 , R-1 , S-1"},{"key":"B","html":"P-4, Q-1, R-2, S-3"},{"key":"C","html":"P-1, Q-2, R-4 , S-3"},{"key":"D","html":"P-3, Q-1 , R- 4, S-2"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\n&bull; Typical applications of EBM are gas orifices for pressure-differential devices, rocket-fuel<br />\ninjectors, round or profile shaped holes on sleeve Valves or injection nozzles on diesel engines.<br />\n&bull; LBM is used predominantly to make holes and cut complex contours.<br />\n&bull; PAM is not have any advantage on easy-to-machine materials such as steel, aluminium or<br />\ncopper alloys so it is normally used for difficult to machine materials such as Inconel, hastelloys and Stainless steel,<br />\n&bull; USM is used for machining hard and brittle materials to complex Shapes with good accuracy<br />\nand reasonable surface finish.</p>"},{"n":44,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A cylindrical tank of 1 m diameter is 4 m long and 40 mm thick and is subjected to an internal pressure of 2 MPa. If the axial compressive load of 400 kN is applied on the tank, then increase in capacity of the tank will be<br />\n[Take, <em>E</em> = 200 GPa, and μ = 0.3]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"7.26 × 10<sup>–4</sup> m<sup>3</sup>"},{"key":"B","html":"4.21 × 10<sup>–4</sup> m<sup>3</sup>"},{"key":"C","html":"12.79 × 10<sup>–4</sup> m<sup>3</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"6.42 × 10<sup>–4</sup> m<sup>3</sup>"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ca/cae60f8e27a69b15fe95.png\" /></div>"},{"n":45,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Water in a tank is maintained at a constant head of 4 m. It is discharged through a horizontal pipe 100 m long and 100 mm in diameter. A valve is provided at the end of the pipe to control the discharge. When the valve is half open, the discharge is 12 × 10<sup>–3</sup> m/s, then find the loss coefficient of the valve.<br />\n[Take friction factor of 0.026]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"3.32"},{"key":"B","html":"4.13"},{"key":"C","html":"7.11"},{"key":"D","html":"9.36"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5d/5d6e9d9374a9ad9da72b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":46,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A bracket is welded to a vertical plate by means of two fillet welds as shown in the figure. If the shear-strength of weld material is 150 MPa and FOS = 2, then the size of the weld is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e5/e5873ddc9df8ddfc1dcf.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/de/de2e2c774db2d60f322c.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2b/2b9c84528c37ee2b28b0.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7d/7d0afe5f0707931eec48.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/74/749b982f2d36fe983f79.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ef/ef96237f6b8a50712b27.png\" /></div>"},{"n":47,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A function <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) is defined as <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) = 3<em>x</em><sup>4</sup> – 2<em>x</em><sup>3</sup> – 6<em>x</em><sup>2</sup> + 6x + 1, 0 ≤ <em>x</em> ≤ 2. The minimum value of <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0"},{"key":"B","html":"1"},{"key":"C","html":"2"},{"key":"D","html":"21"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4f/4f663886826555ff7604.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1f6f37e9737571555995.png\" /></div>"},{"n":48,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The eigen values of the matrix <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/2d/2d583fc858cc3216c7b6.png\" /> are in ratio 1 : 1 : 4. If ‘a’ is a positive real number, then the value of ‘<em>a</em>’ will be ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[6,6],"answerText":"6","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>6 (6 - 6)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/db/db2911624ea569caa8ad.png\" /></div>"},{"n":49,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The percentage change in efficiency of Pelton wheel , if blade speed changes from 45% of incoming jet speed with blade friction coefficient of 0.95 to 55% of incoming jet speed with blade friction coefficient 0.90 is ________ % (Correct upto two decimal places)<br />\n[Take exit blade angle as 15°]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-2.6,-2.4],"answerText":"-2.52","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-2.52 (-2.60 - -2.40)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3f/3f25bdc5508c1aff3c8c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":50,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A cantilever beam of length 3 m (with rigid portion of 1 m at middle) is subjected to a point load of 1 kN at its free end, as shown. If non rigid portion have Young’s modulus of <em>E</em>. The deflection of free end is ______ mm (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/08/08000def0ff3a00b56e0.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>Take <em>E</em> = 200 GPa, <em>I</em> = 8000 × 10<sup>4</sup> mm<sup>4</sup></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.4,0.45],"answerText":"0.42","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.42 (0.40 - 0.45)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e6/e67d656a51f0ecabb166.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d1/d1d5be9fe7de42ffcf85.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fc8dbb4be6d161cef4cc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":51,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The crankpin circle radius of a horizontal engine is 150 mm. The mass of the reciprocating parts is 250 kg. When the crank has traversed 45° from IDC, the difference between the driving and back pressure is 0.35 N/mm<sup>2</sup>. The connecting rod length between centres is 0.6 m and the cylinder bore is 0.25 m. If the engine runs at 300 rpm and the effect of piston rod diameter is neglected then the pressure on the slide bar is ______ kN. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.58,1.66],"answerText":"1.61","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.61 (1.58 - 1.66)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a5/a50a54bf38db3e4b1f0b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A brake drum of 400 mm diameter is braked by a cast iron shoe having a coefficient of friction 0.3. The force is applied at 800 mm away from center line of the drum as shown in figure. The pivot is 300 mm away from central axis on the other side and 10 mm below the surface of drum.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1d/1de92135febfaedbf7f8.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>For applying a braking torque of 500 Nm, the magnitude of the difference in required force <em>F</em> for clockwise and anti-clockwise rotation will be ______ N. [Correct upto two decimal places]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[44.45,46.45],"answerText":"45.45","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>45.45 (44.45 - 46.45)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/96/967c5f506258c251dbef.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":53,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The precedence relationship for Eight-activities is given below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/76/7630df914c3e9c8bb4ac.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The ratio of Free float to Independent float of activity ‘<em>H</em>’ is ___. (Correct upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.75,1.75],"answerText":"1.75","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.75</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a4/a444af9f0882848c1ffc.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":54,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Water flowing through a pipe of diameter 200 mm with a nozzle at the exit having exit diameter 100 mm. The velocity of water in the pipe is 1 m/s. The absolute pressure in the pipe is 200 kPa and atmospheric pressure is 100 kPa.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6aae53dcd1c903f67a5c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The horizontal clamping force (<em>F</em>) required to hold the pipe is _____ kN. (Correct upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5.35,5.45],"answerText":"5.40","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>5.40 (5.35 - 5.45)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fb/fbe73dd01a5fa075a7f1.png\" /></div>"},{"n":55,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A thin tube is of 5 cm mean diameter, 0.25 cm thick, and 100 cm long. The torsional strength (N-m) per unit weight (N) of tube is _____ m. (Correct upto one decimal place) [Take shear strength of shaft material as 160 MPa, ρ = 7800 kg/m<sup>3</sup> and FOS as 4]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[12.8,13.4],"answerText":"13.1","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>13.1 (12.8 - 13.4)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ac/acc36cf02f9f4dde8979.png\" /></div>"},{"n":56,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>For a top gated steel casting, the gating ratio is 1 : 2 : 1.5. A steel casting of mass 50 kg is to be produced with density 2600 kg/m<sup>3</sup>. The pouring time is 15 sec and sprue height is 250 mm. If the efficiency factor is 0.89, then the diameter of the in-gate is ______ cm. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3.46,3.58],"answerText":"3.52","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3.52 (3.46 - 3.58)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9c/9ca10a1cbd121b95fbe8.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c0/c0dc5f8f7292f59ddb29.png\" /></div>"},{"n":57,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A shell and tube heat exchanger is used to condensate an organic vapour at a rate of 500 kg/min at its saturation temperature of 355 K. Cooling water at 286 K is available with a mass flow rate of 60 kg/s. The overall heat transfer coefficient is 475 W/m<sup>2</sup>K and the latent heat of condensation of the vapour is 600 kJ/kg. The logarithmic mean temperature difference (LMTD) for this heat exchanger is ______ °C. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[58.2,58.7],"answerText":"58.49","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>58.49 (58.20 - 58.70)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1fa81dd3baf12504636d.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":58,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A frictionless vertical piston-cylinder assembly fitted with an electrical resistor contains air. The mass and face area of the piston are 60 kg and 0.2 m<sup>2</sup> respectively. The atmospheric pressure is 100 kPa. Electric current is passed through the resistor causing an increase of 0.06 m<sup>3</sup> in the<br />\nvolume of air. The mass of air is 0.5 kg. Due of heating, the specific internal energy of the air increases by 45 kJ/kg. Assuming the assembly to be insulated. The heat transfer from the resistor to the system (air and the piston) is _____ kJ. [Correct upto three decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[28.61,28.699],"answerText":"28.677","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>28.677 (28.610 - 28.699)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f67b14b164891a53f9b7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":59,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>An ammonia refrigerator works between –5°C and 27°C. The vapour is dry saturated at the end of compression. If the power required to drive the compressor is 2.7 kW.<br />\nUse the following properties of NH<sub>3</sub> :</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1b/1b145e3f3c34198e27be.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The cooling capacity of the refrigerator is ________ tons. [Correct upto one decimal place]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[4.2,4.8],"answerText":"4.5","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>4.5 (4.2 - 4.8)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b2/b2a610a9b4f7e05d3439.png\" /></div>"},{"n":60,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A steam power plant operates on an Rankine cycle with superheat. The boiler pressure is 5 MPa and the boiler exit temperature is 600°C. The boiler receives heat from a source at 700°C. The ambient air at 20°C provides cooling in order to maintain the condenser at 45°C. All components are ideal. The processes in all the four components are steady state processes with negligible changes in kinetic and potential energies. Assume that the pump handles an incompressible liquid of specific volume 0.00101 m<sup>3</sup>/kg.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0b/0b24d2d55867560ab9e7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The following thermodynamic properties of water may be useful:\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e3/e389e36147c0cef2c6b7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/ae58ba0881e7b91df30a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The specific steam consumption of plant is ______ kg/kWh. (Correct upto three decimal places)</div>\n</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.63,2.638],"answerText":"2.634","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.634 (2.630 - 2.638)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7b/7b58d4dc62ee2c8fcef5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":61,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The arms of Hartnell governor are of equal length. The mass of each ball is 8.2 kg. The midposition speed (when arms are vertical) is 360 rpm. The extreme radii of rotation are 90 mm and 60 mm respectively. The maximum variation of speed, including sleeve friction is 6% of midposition speed. The sleeve mass is 5 kg and the friction at the sleeve is 35 N. Which of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Spring stiffness is 35.045 N/mm"},{"key":"B","html":"Initial compression is 34.86 mm"},{"key":"C","html":"Maximum spring force is 1223.2 N"},{"key":"D","html":"Data is insufficient for calculation of spring stiffness."}],"answer":["A","B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fb/fbdf092eac23a6a7af99.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b2/b2a8e4c8362667b3ff3b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":62,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The voltage length characteristic of a DC arc welding is given by V = (20 + 4l) volts, where l is the length of arc in mm. The arc length varies between 0.4 cm and 0.6 cm. The power source characteristic is given by <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/be/bec8ea338e2225283653.png\" /> then the welding current for the arc length variation will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"626 A for 0.4 cm"},{"key":"B","html":"670 A for 0.4 cm"},{"key":"C","html":"670 A for 0.6 cm"},{"key":"D","html":"626 A for 0.6 cm"}],"answer":["B","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(b, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6e/6e54eb498cecf1be161c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":63,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Two persons <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> toss an unbiased coin alternatively and whoever gets the first head, wins the game. If <em>A</em> starts the game, then the ratio of probabilities of <em>A</em>’s winning to <em>B</em>’s winning is _______.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2 (2 - 2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/46/467d023d95970895050e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":64,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>It is given that the solution of the differential equation <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/53/53b66557dd2e9db094f0.png\" /> passes through origin. The value of y(2) will be ________. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[6.3,6.5],"answerText":"6.40","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>6.40 (6.30 - 6.50)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/90/906b5d90419b60f06779.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":65,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The velocity of a particle starting from rest is given at different instants as shown in the table below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b5/b5e5cba516c1f78d839f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>Here, time <em>t</em> is in minutes and velocity <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/e5/e5f55f87f1532d7bfe5f.png\" /> is in m/mins. Using Simpson’s <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6ad9b02cd2116bb523f6.png\" /> rule, the distance travelled by the particle in 20 minutes is ________ m. (Correct upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[308,311],"answerText":"309.33","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>309.33 (308.00 - 311.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/35/353dffdc636dc2d5c9be.png\" /></div>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":32,"NAT":29,"MSQ":4},"withoutKey":0}};
